pp wrote:
> I am using 5.1A, the hostname shows only the hostname without domain 
> name. but in /etc/rc.config file, I have defined
> HOSTNAME="abc.domain.com"
> 
> #hostname only shows "abc".
> 
> Can anyone tell me what makes that issue? and where in the system file I 
> can change hostname return abc.domain.com?

If you've changed /etc/rc.config, but not rebooted or restarted the 
network, then the change hasn't taken affect.  You can simply run:

# hostname abc.domain.com

which will set the hostname on the system.

You might also want to check that hostname isn't an alias for 'hostname -s'.

-Brian


