mount -o extend has nothing to do with addvol.  The extend feature 
was implemented to allow an existing volume to be increased in 
size, as in a SAN or RAID controller increasing the size of an 
individual LUN.

Doing an addvol should just increase the amount of storage 
available in the domain right away.  No need to do anything else.

However if fileset quotas are in place, then the fileset will be 
limited on the amount of storage in the domain it is allowed to 
use.  Remember a domain may contain multiple filesets, and fileset 
quotas are a way to make sure that a some or all of the filesets 
sharing a domain do not use all the space.
<http://h30097.www3.hp.com/docs/base_doc/DOCUMENTATION/V51B_HTML/AR
H96DTE/TITLE.HTM>

                                        Bob Harris

                                        Bob Harris


